Id: mac002w
Severity: WARN
Category: kernel
Check: check_mac
References: selinux(8), setenforce(8)

SELinux is loaded but in permissive mode: it logs every access its
policy would deny and denies none of them, so it protects nothing.
Permissive mode is for finding what a policy would break, briefly.

To fix it, look at what was logged ('ausearch -m avc -ts recent', or
'sealert -a /var/log/audit/audit.log'), fix the labels or booleans it
points at, then 'setenforce 1' and set SELINUX=enforcing in
/etc/selinux/config so it stays that way after a reboot. One domain can
be left permissive ('semanage permissive -a DOMAIN') while the rest
enforces.
